But where is the ce'u in "ni ko'a xunre"? If you agree with me on ce'u,
you agree that "ni ko'a xunre" is as bad as "ka ko'a xunre"; really bad.

I have disagreed on ce'u in the past, but more or less am willing to accede 
to what others seem to have decided (but I'll have to see how my personal 
idiolect works out). If you want to use "ni ce'u xunre", and others agree, 
I'll understand it.



